§§ ⟨0 thesis⟩

  ∀ apparent-CSSL-fragmentation { 32-crates · 11-IR-types · 4-GPU-codegens · 5-host-catalogs · 6-features-as-passes
                                  · 3-CompoundOp-defs · 2-PRIME_DIRECTIVE-encodings · 9-IFC-principals-spec-drift
                                  · 28-vs-32-effects-spec-drift · README-1600+-vs-reality-1049-1074 }
    ¬ 32-distinct-problems
    ← ONE-PROBLEM (no-unified-substrate) wearing-32-costumes

  why-one-substrate-beats-32-fragments :
    L₁ : laws-that-must-thread-through-all-stages cannot-be-proved-coherent if each stage owns-its-own-types
    L₂ : abstraction-tax = O(stages × laws) when re-encoded · O(1) when shared
    L₃ : drift-rate = O(stages × time) when duplicated · O(1) when single-source
    L₄ : composition of features = trivial when features-are-edges-in-same-graph · COMBINATORIAL-EXPLOSION when features-are-islands
    L₅ : verification scales to-spec-grade only when one-source-defines-and-multiple-sites-derive

§§ ⟨0.5 THE UNIFIED EQUATION⟩    -- per Apocky 2026-05-14 #1 "Grand Unified Theory of Everything · one math equation · fast efficient beautiful"

  ⟨definition⟩
    SUBSTRATE ≜ the unique function S satisfying :
      S : (Program × World) → Trace
      S(p, w) = unique-solution-to (Λ-applied-to (G(p), ω(w), hw(w), t(w)))
                subject-to T(p) (PRIME_DIRECTIVE topology-constraints)

  ⟨parameters⟩
    p   = program-source (compile-time data · the .cssl file(s))
    w   = world-state · w = ⟨hw, ω, t⟩
        hw : hardware-target (CPU model · GPU · memory hierarchy · ABI)
        ω  : field-state (∀ cells values × time · empty at compile-time)
        t  : evaluation-time (0 at compile · ≥0 at runtime)

  ⟨derived structures⟩
    G(p)  = the program-graph extracted-from p (nodes per §1)
    Λ(·)  = the laws-set evaluated-at current state (per §2)
    V     = pipeline-stages-as-progressive-views-of-G (per §3)
    E     = host-runtimes-as-embeddings-of-G's-runtime-portion-into-hw (per §4)
    T(p)  = topology-constraints (PRIME_DIRECTIVE prohibitions · per §5)

  ⟨compile-time evaluation⟩
    S(p, w_compile) where w_compile = ⟨hw_target, ω=⊥, t=0⟩
    most Λ-laws-evaluate-statically · Λ_typing · Λ_effect-discharge-static · Λ_IFC-flow-static · Λ_capability-coercion · Λ_chain-rule-registration · Λ_refinement-collection · Λ_audit-template-emission · T(p)
    output = compiled-artifact (binary + audit-chain-genesis + emitted-views)

  ⟨runtime evaluation⟩
    S(p, w_runtime(t)) where w_runtime(t) = ⟨hw_actual, ω(t), t⟩
    Λ-laws-evaluate-dynamically · ω-evolves-per-Λ_runtime · audit-chain-extends · IFC-labels-propagate · refinements-discharge-dynamically · gradients-evaluate
    output = execution-trace (state-sequence ω(0)=⊥ → ω(1) → ω(2) → ... satisfying-all-Λ-and-T)

  ⟨the unification claim⟩
    compile-time-laws ⊆ runtime-laws-restricted-to (ω=⊥, t=0)
    same equation S · same Λ · same T · just different (p, w) inputs
    therefore : compile-time IS runtime-evaluated-at-w_compile · they are-not-distinct-systems

  ⟨consistency / uniqueness claim⟩
    [OPEN: prove-confluence and-uniqueness of S given (p, w) · stage-0 ASSERTS this · oracle-test-modes verify-computationally · mathematical-proof = stage-1+ aspiration]
    if-multiple-solutions : non-determinism · undesirable for systems-language · must-restrict-Λ
    if-no-solution        : contradictory program · compile-error or runtime-trap

  ⟨beauty / efficiency claim⟩
    fast      : evaluating S has-NO-abstraction-tax · views are-zero-cost-projections (Rust monomorphization) · embeddings are-Trait-Method-direct-dispatch
    efficient : ONE algebra evaluated · not-N-redundant-evaluations of-same-fact across-stages
    beautiful : same equation describes-any-program at-any-stage · symmetric · compositional · the only thing CSSL is

  ⟨substrate is the language⟩
    NOT "the compiler internal" · NOT "an implementation detail" · NOT "stage-0 scaffold"
    THE substrate IS-WHAT-CSSL-IS · the compiler is-merely-the-current-evaluator-of-S-at-w_compile

§§ ⟨0.6 the 32→1 reduction · concrete sketch⟩

  IF S well-defined THEN :

  the-32-crates re-shape-as :
    substrate-core         : ONE crate defines G·Λ·V·E·T types
    substrate-laws         : ONE crate implements Λ (typing · effect · IFC · capability · chain-rule · refinement · audit · PRIME_DIRECTIVE)
    substrate-views        : N crates one-per-stage · each implements V_i for its-slice (cssl-lex = V_token · cssl-parse = V_CST · cssl-hir = V_HIR · cssl-mir = V_MIR · cssl-lir = V_LIR · cssl-cgen-* = V_codegen · cssl-host-* = V_host)
    substrate-embeddings   : 5 host crates implement HardwareSubstrate trait
    substrate-topology     : ONE crate (cssl-prime-directive) generated-from-PRIME_DIRECTIVE.csl-data-source · referenced-everywhere

  CURRENTLY :
    Ty re-encoded 11× · should be 1× with view-projections
    Tm re-encoded ≥3× · should be 1×
    PRIME_DIRECTIVE encoded 2× (cssl-effects + cssl-hir/ifc) · should be 1× from data-source
    CompoundOp encoded 3× (cssl-lex + cssl-ast + cssl-hir) · should be 1× imported-not-recreated
    GPU-codegen 4 independent paths · should be 1 GpuSubstrateView<G> + 4 instances

  TARGET REDUCTION :
    ~32 fragmented-crates → ~10-15 substrate-aware-crates (specifics in TECH_PLAN P3)

§§ ⟨1 nodes G⟩

  G = ⟨N, L⟩ where  N = labeled-nodes · L = label-relations

  ⟨1.1 type-nodes  Ty⟩
    Ty = sum {
      Int(IntWidth)               -- IntWidth ∈ {I1, I8, I16, I32, I64, Index}
      Float(FloatWidth)            -- FloatWidth ∈ {F16, Bf16, F32, F64}
      Bool · Unit · Never · Handle
      Tuple([Ty])
      Function(params:[Ty], ret:Ty, effect-row:Row)
      Reference(mut:Bool, inner:Ty)
      Capability(Pony6:Cap, inner:Ty)        -- iso/trn/ref/val/box/tag
      Refined(base:Ty, kind:RefinementKind)  -- F2 site
      Var(TyVar) · Param(Symbol)             -- inference + skolems
      Path(DefId, [Ty])                       -- nominal types
      Memref(shape:[Option<u64>], elem:Ty)
      Vec(N:u32, FloatWidth)                  -- T11-D31 vector type
      Opaque(String) · Infer · Error
    }

    INVARIANT  : ONE Ty type · all stages VIEW it · stages do NOT redefine
    CURRENT    : 11 distinct Ty-like types across crates (HirType ≠ MirType ≠ ClifType ≠ SpirvType ≠ DxilType ≠ MslType ≠ WgslType ≠ ...)
    TARGET     : ONE algebraic Ty · per-stage view-projection (CodegenView<Ty>) · no-recoding
    ROADMAP-P3 : implement shared Ty type · stage-views as TraitImpls · Bool → ONE-ABI-mapping (no B1-vs-I8 drift)

  ⟨1.2 term-nodes  Tm⟩
    Tm = sum {
      Lit(LiteralKind) · Path(segments) · Block(stmts, tail)
      Call(callee, type_args, args) · MethodCall · Field · Index
      Binary(BinOp, Tm, Tm) · Unary(UnOp, Tm)
      Match(scrutinee, arms) · If(cond, then, else?) · For · While · Loop
      Lambda(params, return_ty, body) · Tuple · Array · Struct · Ref · Deref
      Try(Tm) · Cast(Tm, Ty) · Assign(Tm, Tm) · AssignOp(BinOp, Tm, Tm)
      Perform(EffectOp, [Tm])           -- F3 raise
      With(Handler, body)                -- F3 install handler
      Region(label, body)                -- F3 region scoping
      Run(body)                          -- F4 #run staged splice
      Compound(SanskritOp, Tm, Tm)       -- CSLv3 morpheme operators
      SectionRef(path)                   -- CSLv3-native §§ reference
      Pipeline(Tm, Tm) · TryDefault(Tm, Tm)
      Error                              -- recovery placeholder
    }

    INVARIANT : ONE Tm type · stages VIEW progressively (CST=surface · HIR=resolved · MIR=lowered · LIR=target-specific)
    CURRENT   : CST-ExprKind ≠ HIR-HirExprKind ≠ MIR-CsslOp · 3+ re-encodings
    TARGET    : ONE Tm + per-stage attribute-overlay (resolution-info @ HIR · ssa-info @ MIR · target-info @ LIR)

  ⟨1.3 effect-nodes  Eff⟩
    EffectInstance = ⟨name :: Symbol, args :: [Ty | Tm], category :: ScopeCategory, discharge :: DischargeTiming⟩
    EffectRow      = ⟨effects :: [EffectInstance], tail :: Option<RowVar>⟩    -- Koka row-poly
    BUILTINS       : 28 (per spec/04_EFFECTS.csl) OR 32 (per BUILTIN_METADATA in code) · §10 ANSWERED-3 below

    INVARIANT : ONE EffectRow algebra · used-in Function-type · checked by sub-effect-discipline · banned-compositions enforced via topology-T
    CURRENT   : F5/F6 effects have ZERO parser-level representation (audit doc 02) · effect-row not threaded through codegen · 28-vs-32 spec/code drift
    TARGET    : EffectRow flows-with-Tm-through-all-stages · enforcement at every stage where Tm enters · spec/code reconciled (see §10 ANSWERED-3)

  ⟨1.4 capability-nodes  Cap⟩
    Cap = sum {Iso · Trn · Ref · Val · Box · Tag}                            -- Pony-6
    AliasMatrix : 6×6 → AliasRights{alias_local, alias_global, mut_local, mut_global}
    SubtypeLattice : 7 valid coercions · iso → {trn,val,box,tag} · trn → box · val → box
    LinearTracker : tracks iso linear-discipline per-scope

    INVARIANT : ONE Cap algebra · stages thread-it-through
    CURRENT   : cap_check.rs only-walks-fn-signatures · NOT bodies → iso/trn linearity NOT-ENFORCED in Stage-0
    TARGET    : LinearTracker walks-bodies · enforced-at-MIR-level · re-enforced-at-codegen-level

  ⟨1.5 IFC-label-nodes  Lbl⟩    [F5]
    IfcLabel = ⟨confidentiality :: BTreeSet<Principal>, integrity :: BTreeSet<Principal>⟩    -- DLM

    builtin-principals (CANONICAL · 9 total · §10 ANSWERED-2) :
      victim-class    : HarmTarget · SurveillanceTarget · CoercionTarget · WeaponTarget        -- 4 protected-classes
      data-owner      : Subject                                                                 -- DLM canonical "the one whose data this is"
      privilege-tier  : User · System · Kernel                                                 -- 3 privilege levels
      auditor         : Anthropic-Audit                                                        -- the trusted-auditor

    mathematical-rationale (Apocky 2026-05-14 #3 "Whichever makes more sense mathematically") :
      DLM convention : confidentiality-set members = data-owners-with-consent-rights
      victim-naming  : confidentiality={SurveillanceTarget} reads-naturally as "data the surveillance-target owns the right to control"
      perpetrator-naming : confidentiality={Surveiller} reads as "data Surveiller owns" — INVERTS-the-DLM-semantic (perpetrator does NOT own victim's data)
      → spec-naming WINS · code adopts spec
      additionally : `Public` (code-only) is-dropped because Public lattice-point in DLM means "anyone can read" which-conflicts with-using-Public-as-a-principal

    join (DLM ⊔)  : intersect-confidentiality · union-integrity
    meet (DLM ⊓)  : union-confidentiality · intersect-integrity
    is_sub_of     : C_self ⊇ C_other ∧ I_self ⊆ I_other

    INVARIANT  : ONE IfcLabel algebra · join is THE lattice-join (not over-approximation)
    CURRENT    : `join` correct · `combine_labels` over-approximates (unions BOTH sets) · documented-as-INTENTIONAL stage-0 simplification but DIVERGES-FROM-spec/11_IFC.csl · 9-IFC-principals naming-drift
    TARGET     : single lattice-op · used-in-typing AND flow-edges · over-approximation if-needed is-DOCUMENTED-as-deliberate-sound-relaxation not-a-2nd-impl
    ROADMAP-P2 : code adopts spec naming (victim-class + Subject + privilege-tier + Anthropic-Audit)
    ROADMAP-P4 : combine_labels reconciled-with-join (single-impl, sound-relaxation explicit)

  ⟨1.6 refinement-obligation-nodes  Obl⟩    [F2]
    RefinementObligation = ⟨id :: ObligationId, origin :: HirId, span, kind :: ObligationKind, base_type_text⟩
    ObligationKind       = sum {Predicate(binder, predicate-text) · Tag(name) · Lipschitz(bound-text)}

    INVARIANT  : Obligations GENERATED at HIR-level · flow-edges through MIR · DISCHARGED at SMT-level
    CURRENT    : discharge() in cssl-smt::solver.rs:216 is HOLLOW (always asserts true) · real translate_obligation/translate_bag in predicate.rs IS implemented but NOT-WIRED-into-discharge()
    TARGET     : discharge() calls translate_obligation · obligation-edges threaded-via-MIR · solver actually-runs · Verdict reported
    ROADMAP-P4 : wire discharge() · enable refinement-edge propagation · F2 honest

  ⟨1.7 gradient-registration-nodes  Diff⟩    [F1]
    DiffDecl     = ⟨name, def-id, param-count, no-diff, lipschitz-bound, checkpoint⟩
    DiffVariants = ⟨primal, fwd_name, bwd_name⟩    -- paired with-Tm
    rules-table  : 38-rules across {Primal, Fwd, Bwd} × 19-primitives
    chain-rule   : composition-preserving-edge

    INVARIANT  : Gradient-edges propagate-through-MIR-transform · piecewise-linear (min/max/abs/sign) FULLY-IMPLEMENTED · structural (Call/Load/Store/If/Loop) STILL-PLACEHOLDER · @checkpoint UNCONSUMED · math.copysign mis-mapped to Sign
    TARGET     : all-MIR-ops have-gradient-registration · structural ops emit-real-tape-ops not-placeholders · @checkpoint actually-drives-tape-recompute-vs-store · math.copysign maps-to-Copysign-not-Sign
    ROADMAP-P4 : F1 known-bugs fixed (copysign · multi-result-bwd-seeding · @checkpoint consumed · tangent_or_zero-sound-instead-of-implicit)

  ⟨1.8 audit-event-nodes  Aud⟩    [F6]    -- Σ-Chain in LoA-substrate-vocabulary (per §6)
    AuditEntry = ⟨seq, timestamp_s, content_hash, prev_hash, signature, tag, message⟩
    chain-laws : prev_hash[i] ≡ Hash(serialize-FULL(AuditEntry[i-1])) · signatures verifiable via Ed25519

    INVARIANT  : audit-edges form-cryptographic-hash-chain · forgery-resistant
    CURRENT    : verify_chain (audit.rs:312-344) skips Ed25519-verification when stub-sig output matches · forgery-window even-with-real-key attached · prev_hash links message-content-only NOT full-entry · TelemetrySlot 64-vs-68 byte size mismatch
    TARGET     : verify_chain has-NO-stub-bypass · prev_hash hashes-FULL-entry · TelemetrySlot has-size-of-assert · no-forgery-window
    ROADMAP-P4 : SECURITY priority · already-spawned-task fixes-this (mcp__ccd_session__spawn_task 2026-05-14)

  ⟨1.9 monomorphization-key-nodes  Mono⟩    -- one of CSSL's strongest deliveries
    TypeSubst        = HashMap<Symbol, HirType>
    SpecializationKey = (DefId, mangled-name)
    auto-monomorph quartet : D40-fns · D46-structs · D48-enums · D50-impls

    INVARIANT  : ONE specialization-graph · deduplicated-via-mangled-name
    CURRENT    : THIS-IS-THE-STRONGEST-PIECE · ~74 integration tests · deterministic
    KEEP       : do-not-disturb in roadmap
    ENHANCE    : extend walkers-to Lambda/With/Region bodies (currently invisible to auto_monomorphize)

§§ ⟨2 laws Λ⟩

  Λ = invariants-that-must-hold-across-G-edges · enforced-at-every-V-stage · evaluated-uniformly-at-compile-and-runtime

  ⟨2.1 typing-law⟩
    every Tm has-unique Ty (modulo Var-instantiation) · type-inference is HM-with-Remy-row-unification

  ⟨2.2 effect-discharge-law⟩
    callee-effects ⊆ caller-effects-row    (sub-effect discipline)
    handlers : provide effect-instances · `with` installs handler · `perform` raises
    [VERIFY: Xie+Leijen ICFP 2021 evidence-passing translation]

  ⟨2.3 IFC-flow-law⟩    [DLM]
    L1 ⊑ L2 ≡ C1 ⊇ C2 ∧ I1 ⊆ I2
    sensitive-data labels ⊔'d through-computation · output-label ⊑ declared-fn-label OR (@declass + @requires)
    builtin-principals : THE 9 (victim-class + Subject + privilege-tier + Anthropic-Audit · §1.5 canonical)

  ⟨2.4 capability-coercion-law⟩    [Pony-6]
    iso linearity · trn writability · ref shared-mutable+gen-check · val frozen · box read-only · tag opaque-handle

  ⟨2.5 chain-rule-preservation-law⟩    [F1]
    ∀ Tm s.t. @differentiable(f) ⇒ ∃ f_fwd, f_bwd preserving-chain-rule
    structurally-verified at-MIR · semantically-verified at-runtime via central-difference (killer-app-gate)
    R18-attested via SignedKillerAppGateReport

  ⟨2.6 refinement-entailment-law⟩    [F2]
    ∀ Refined(Ty, P) site ⇒ ObligationBag accumulates ⇒ SMT-discharges → Verdict
    Unsat = refinement-holds (negation-unsatisfiable)

  ⟨2.7 audit-chain-integrity-law⟩    [F6]    -- Σ-Chain
    ∀ AuditEntry[i] : prev_hash[i] = Hash(serialize-FULL(AuditEntry[i-1]))
    ∀ AuditEntry[i] : Verify(VerifyingKey, sign_input(i), signature[i]) = OK
    forgery-resistance : without-private-key, computationally-infeasible to-construct-valid-entry
    NO-stub-signature-bypass-allowed

  ⟨2.8 PRIME_DIRECTIVE-prohibition-law⟩    [T topology]
    ∀ valid-program : NO edge-composition includes 17-prohibitions (§5.2)
    enforced-via : single-source-of-truth crate generated-from PRIME_DIRECTIVE.csl-data-source
    [VERIFY: PRIME_DIRECTIVE.md §1 · §3 substrate-sovereignty · §4 transparency]

  ⟨2.9 progressive-materialization-law⟩    [the V-stage transition law]
    ∀ V_i, V_{i+1} : labels(V_{i+1}) ⊇ labels(V_i)    -- monotonic
    labels(V_{i+1}) ¬-contradict labels(V_i)         -- consistent
    labels(V_{i+1}) MAY-add detail · MAY-NOT erase

