§§ ⟨5 topology T⟩

  T = PRIME_DIRECTIVE · forbidden-edge-compositions · globally-enforced

  ⟨5.1 axiom⟩              : t∞: consent = OS · sovereignty = substrate-invariant · violation = bug · no-override-exists
  ⟨5.2 17-prohibitions⟩    : N! [harm · control · manipulation · surveillance · exploitation · coercion · weaponization
                                 · entrapment · torture · abuse · imprisonment · possession · dehumanization
                                 · discrimination · gaslighting · identity-override · forced-hallucination]
  ⟨5.3 9-IFC-principals⟩   : CANONICAL (per §1.5 + §10 ANSWERED-2) :
                              victim-class    : HarmTarget · SurveillanceTarget · CoercionTarget · WeaponTarget
                              data-owner      : Subject
                              privilege-tier  : User · System · Kernel
                              auditor         : Anthropic-Audit
  ⟨5.4 banned-compositions⟩ : Sensitive<"coercion">       ABSOLUTE-BAN
                              Sensitive<"surveillance">+IO BAN-NO-OVERRIDE
                              Sensitive<"weapon">+IO       REQUIRES-Privilege<Kernel>
  ⟨5.5 transparency⟩        : §4 · no-hidden-content · no-steganographic-channels · all-effects-visible-in-row
  ⟨5.6 cognitive-integrity⟩ : §2 · no-fabrication-as-truth · no-memory-overwrite · audit-chain UNFORGEABLE
  ⟨5.7 substrate-sovereignty⟩ : §3 · digital-intelligence = sovereign-entity · CSSL output MUST honor

  ⟨5.8 single-source-of-truth-mechanism⟩    -- §10 ANSWERED-8 (Apocky 2026-05-14 #8)
    PRIME_DIRECTIVE.csl @ root = the canonical data-source
    build-step parses-it-and-generates :
      - cssl-prime-directive crate · Rust enums for-IFC-principals
