§§ ⟨8 design-laws-the-roadmap-must-honor⟩

  L1 substrate-first      : every-contribution MUST-reduce-not-increase orthogonal-abstractions
  L2 stages-as-views      : each-stage materializes-MORE-of-G · NEVER re-encodes
  L3 features-as-edges    : each F1-F6 IS-an-edge-class-in-Λ · features-compose because-they're-in-same-graph
  L4 hosts-as-embeddings  : each-host IS-an-instance-of HardwareSubstrate<G>-trait
  L5 topology-as-single-source : T enforced ONCE in-cssl-prime-directive (generated-from-PRIME_DIRECTIVE.csl) · referenced-everywhere
  L6 spec-code-coherence  : every spec/code drift IS-a-bug · roadmap-must-include-reconciliation
  L7 LoA-alignment        : compile-time-substrate ≡ runtime-substrate-with-ω-field-empty · always-and-forever
  L8 progressive-materialization : data-flows-DOWN-the-pipeline · NEVER-up-the-fragmentation
  L9 honest-reporting     : compiled ≠ tested ≠ verified-against-spec · never-overclaim · audit-chain-makes-the-honesty-cryptographic
  L10 PRIME_DIRECTIVE-as-immutable-root : §7 immutability · no-override · gates-every-output-of-the-system
  L11 iterate-improve-critically-each-pass    -- per Apocky 2026-05-14 #9
      : EVERY pass (turn · dispatch · synthesis · phase-exit) MUST :
        - challenge-at-least-one previously-held-assumption
        - improve-at-least-one previously-shipped-artifact
        - cite-at-least-one new primary-source-validation OR identify a new [OPEN] worth investigating
      : no-pass is-allowed-to-be-pure-maintenance · iteration is-the-discipline

